  "readme": "# 🚀 CryptoCrowd - Decentralized Crowdfunding Platform\n\nA comprehensive Web3 project implementing a decentralized crowdfunding platform using Solidity, Hardhat, and Chainlink price feeds.\n\n## 🎯 Project Overview\n\nThe FundMe smart contract is a decentralized crowdfunding platform that allows users to contribute ETH to reach a funding target. The contract includes sophisticated features like:\n\n- **Minimum Contribution Threshold**: Ensures meaningful contributions (minimum $100 USD equivalent)\n- **Funding Target**: Set at $1000 USD equivalent\n- **Time-locked Funding Period**: Configurable lock time for the funding window\n- **Automatic Refunds**: Contributors can reclaim their funds if the target isn't met\n- **Chainlink Price Feeds**: Real-time ETH/USD conversion for accurate value tracking\n- **Owner Withdrawal**: Project owner can withdraw funds only if target is reached\n\n## 🏗️ Smart Contract Architecture\n\n### Core Features\n\n1. **Funding Function**: Accepts ETH contributions with minimum value validation\n2. **Investor Tracking**: Records all contributions and contributor addresses\n3. **Target-based Withdrawal**: Owner can withdraw funds only if target is reached within the lock period\n4. **Automatic Refund System**: Contributors can reclaim funds if target isn't met after lock period\n5. **Price Oracle Integration**: Uses Chainlink for accurate ETH/USD conversion\n\n### Key Functions\n\n- [`fund()`](contracts/FundMe.sol:37): Accept ETH contributions with minimum value check\n- [`getFund()`](contracts/FundMe.sol:64): Owner withdrawal function (target must be reached)\n- [`refund()`](contracts/FundMe.sol:81): Contributor refund function (target not reached)\n- [`convertEthToUsd()`](contracts/FundMe.sol:55): Internal ETH to USD conversion using Chainlink\n\n## 🛠️ Technology Stack\n\n- **Solidity**: Smart contract development (v0.8.20)\n- **Hardhat**: Development environment and testing framework\n- **Chainlink**: Price feed oracle for ETH/USD conversion\n- **Ethers.js**: Ethereum library for blockchain interaction\n- **OpenZeppelin**: Secure contract dependencies\n\n## 📋 Prerequisites\n\n- Node.js (v16 or higher)\n- npm or yarn package manager\n- MetaMask or similar Web3 wallet\n- Sepolia testnet ETH for deployment and testing\n\n## 🚀 Installation & Setup\n\n1. **Clone the repository**\n\n   ```bash\n   git clone <repository-url>\n   cd CryptoCrowd\n   ```\n\n2. **Install dependencies**\n\n   ```bash\n   npm install\n   ```\n\n3. **Environment Configuration**\n   Create a `.env` file in the root directory:\n\n   ```env\n   SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=your_sepolia_rpc_url\n   PRIVATE_KEY=your_private_key\n   PRIVATE_KEY_1=second_private_key_for_testing\n   ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=your_etherscan_api_key\n   ```\n\n4. **Compile the contract**\n   ```bash\n   npx hardhat compile\n   ```\n\n## 🔧 Deployment & Interaction\n\n### Deploy Using Script\n\n```bash\nnpx hardhat run scripts/deployFundMe.js --network sepolia\n```\n\n### Deploy Using Hardhat Task\n\n```bash\nnpx hardhat deploy-fundme --network sepolia\n```\n\n### Interact with Deployed Contract\n\n```bash\nnpx hardhat interact-fundme --addr <contract-address> --network sepolia\n```\n\n## 📊 Contract Configuration\n\n### Constructor Parameters\n\n- `_lockTime`: Duration of the funding window (in seconds)\n\n### Constants\n\n- **MINIMUM_VALUE**: $100 USD (in wei equivalent)\n- **TARGET**: $1000 USD (in wei equivalent)\n- **Chainlink Price Feed**: Sepolia testnet ETH/USD oracle\n\n## 🧪 Testing Workflow\n\nThe deployment script automatically performs these actions:\n\n1. **Contract Deployment**: Deploys FundMe with 300-second lock time\n2. **Contract Verification**: Verifies on Etherscan (if configured)\n3. **Funding Simulation**:\n   - First account contributes 0.5 ETH\n   - Second account contributes 0.5 ETH\n4. **Balance Tracking**: Monitors contract and contributor balances\n5. **Mapping Validation**: Verifies contributor amount tracking\n\n## 🔒 Security Features\n\n- **Access Control**: Owner-only functions for sensitive operations\n- **Time-based Restrictions**: Funding window with configurable lock time\n- **Value Validation**: Minimum contribution requirements\n- **Reentrancy Protection**: Safe ETH transfer patterns\n- **Oracle Integration**: Reliable price feeds for accurate valuation\n\n## 📈 Gas Optimization\n\n- Efficient storage patterns using mappings\n- Minimal external calls during funding\n- Optimized price conversion calculations\n- Batch operations for deployment and verification\n\n## 🔗 Network Configuration\n\n**Sepolia Testnet**\n\n- Chain ID: 11155111\n- RPC: Configurable via environment variable\n- Explorer: https://sepolia.etherscan.io\n\n## 📚 Learning Objectives\n\nThis project covers core Web3 development concepts:\n\n1. **Smart Contract Development**: Solidity best practices and patterns\n2. **Oracle Integration**: Chainlink price feed implementation\n3. **Hardhat Framework**: Configuration, tasks, and scripting\n4. **Testing Strategies**: Local and testnet deployment workflows\n5. **Security Considerations**: Access control and value validation\n6. **Gas Optimization**: Efficient contract design patterns\n\n## 🤝 Contributing\n\n1. Fork the repository\n2. Create a feature branch (`git checkout -b feature/amazing-feature`)\n3. Commit your changes (`git commit -m 'Add amazing feature'`)\n4. Push to the branch (`git push origin feature/amazing-feature`)\n5. Open a Pull Request\n\n## 📝 License\n\nThis project is licensed under the MIT License - see the [LICENSE](LICENSE) file for details.\n\n## 🆘 Support\n\nFor questions and support:\n\n- Create an issue in the repository\n- Check the Hardhat documentation: https://hardhat.org/docs\n- Review Chainlink documentation: https://docs.chain.link\n\n## 🔗 Additional Resources\n\n- [Solidity Documentation](https://docs.soliditylang.org/)\n- [Hardhat Documentation](https://hardhat.org/docs)\n- [Chainlink Price Feeds](https://docs.chain.link/data-feeds)\n- [Ethereum Development Guide](https://ethereum.org/en/developers/)\n\n---\n\n**Happy Building!** 🚀\n",
